/**
 * Process-wide module loaders for authored agent files.
 *
 * The CLI dynamically imports user TypeScript (`agent/agent.ts`,
 * `agent/tools/*.ts`, `evals/**\/*.eval.ts`) at runtime, and plain Node
 * cannot load `.ts` modules. Instead of requiring hosts to wrap the bin in
 * `node --import tsx`, the bin (and programmatic `serve()`) registers tsx's
 * ESM loader itself on startup.
 *
 * On compiled runs it additionally registers alias hooks so authored bare
 * imports of the framework (`@grok/agent-sdk[/x]`) short-circuit to the same
 * files the CLI loaded. Channel option WeakMaps
 * (`getGitHubChannelOptions`, …) require that identity; letting tsx path-map
 * or a second install win loads a duplicate module and breaks continuation /
 * hosted-delivery lookups. Bare npm deps from monorepo `packages/agent-serve/`
 * source still retry against this package (hosted factory engines).
 * Source runs (tsx from the monorepo) skip both — the host loader and
 * tsconfig paths already cover them — and register only source-only exports.
 */
